Rule 1 (torch.jit.is_tracing API with boolean output)
{v_1 : bool} |= v_1 = true ∨ v_1 = false
>>
Rule 2 (torch.jit.is_tracing API always return a boolean, represented by 0 or 1)
{v_1 : int} |= v_1 = 0 ∨ v_1 = 1
>>
Rule 3 (is_tracing returns True if tracing else false)
{ v_1 : bool} |= if v_1 = true then true else false
>>
Rule 4 (is_tracing implies v_2 is 1 if tracing is enabled, 0 otherwise)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : int} |= if v_1 = true then v_2 = 1 else v_2 = 0
>>
Rule 5 (torch.jit.is_tracing API returns a boolean, which can be represented by a string "true" or "false")
{v_1 : str} |= v_1 = "true" ∨ v_1 = "false"
>>
Rule 6 (if tracing is disabled then another boolean variable should be false)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : bool} |= if v_1 = false then v_2 = false
>>
Rule 7 (is_tracing can only be called during JIT compilation, otherwise, another variable must be false)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : bool} |= if v_1 = true then v_2 = true else v_2 = false
>>
Rule 8 (a string variable must be "true" when tracing is enabled)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : str} |= if v_1 = true then v_2 = "true"
>>
Rule 9 (tracing enabled and another boolean is false is impossible)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : bool} |= if v_1 = true then v_2 ≠ false
>>
Rule 10 (Tracing being false implies the result should never be true)
{v_1 : bool} |= if v_1 = false then v_1 ≠ true
>>
Rule 11 (When tracing is enabled, a tensor variable should not be empty)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 = true then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) > 0
>>
Rule 12 (When tracing is disabled, min of a tensor should be less than or equal to max)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 = false then min(v_2) ≤ max(v_2)
>>
Rule 13 (If is_tracing returns false then any string should not be "tanh")
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : str} |= if v_1 = false then v_2 ≠ "tanh"
>>
Rule 14 (If tracing is enabled, all elements in a list of floats should be above 0)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : list(float)} |= if v_1 = true then ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : v_2[i] > 0
>>
Rule 15 (If tracing is true, then all dtypes in a list of dtypes must match)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : list(dtype)} |= if v_1 = true then ∀i ∈ [1, v_2.len - 1] : v_2[i] = v_2[0]
>>
Rule 16 (If is_tracing is enabled then a given tuple should have same len as a tensor's dimension)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tuple(int)} |= if v_1 = true then v_3.len = ndim(v_2)
>>
Rule 17 (If is_tracing returns true, then shape of the given tensor should be greater than zero)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 = true then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) > 0
>>
Rule 18 (is_tracing returns true, if another bool is true or an int is above zero)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : bool, v_3 : int} |= if v_1 = true then v_2 = true ∨ v_3 > 0
>>
Rule 19 (If tracing then max value of tensor must be less than some float)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : float} |= if v_1 = true then max(v_2) < v_3
>>
Rule 20 (If not tracing and dtype_ of a tensor is float32, then it should be equal to 7)
{v_1: bool, v_2: tensor} |= if v_1 = false then dtype_(v_2) = 7
>>
Rule 21 (If is_tracing is true, the shape of tensor v_2 should match tuple v_3)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tuple(int)} |= if v_1 = true then ∀i ∈ [0, v_3.len - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = v_3[i]
